nat44-ed: hairpinned replies leave from the mapped port

When an inside host connects to the outside address and a static mapping
that leads back inside, the new session's o2i flow matches the reply from
the mapped service's inside address and port and rewrites its source address
back to the outside address, but not its source port: the reply left from
the inside port (5003) instead of the mapped one (6003), and the client,
which had sent to 6003, dropped it. Both the dynamic and the static-mapping
branch of slow-path session creation missed it.

Rewrite the source port to the port the client sent to. Without hairpinning
that port is already the one the flow matches, so nat_6t_l3_l4_csum_calc
treats the rewrite as no change.

Verified in an isolated VPP: hairpinned TCP connects and UDP gets its answer
from the mapped port, with in/out interfaces and with the output feature plus
an inside interface; without this patch TCP never connects. Test:
tests/integration/integration_nat44_partial_checksum.py --nat ed.

--- a/src/plugins/nat/nat44-ed/nat44_ed_in2out.c
+++ b/src/plugins/nat/nat44-ed/nat44_ed_in2out.c
@@ -513,6 +513,9 @@
       else
 	{
 	  nat_6t_flow_dport_rewrite_set (&s->o2i, l_port);
+	  /* hairpinning: the reply comes from the mapped service's inside
+	   * port and must leave with the port the client sent to */
+	  nat_6t_flow_sport_rewrite_set (&s->o2i, r_port);
 	}
       nat_6t_flow_txfib_rewrite_set (&s->o2i, rx_fib_index);
       nat_6t_flow_saddr_rewrite_set (&s->o2i, r_addr.as_u32);
@@ -557,6 +560,8 @@
 	  nat_6t_o2i_flow_init (sm, thread_index, s, daddr, dport, sm_addr,
 				sm_port, s->out2in.fib_index, proto);
 	  nat_6t_flow_dport_rewrite_set (&s->o2i, l_port);
+	  /* hairpinning, as above */
+	  nat_6t_flow_sport_rewrite_set (&s->o2i, r_port);
 	}
       nat_6t_flow_daddr_rewrite_set (&s->o2i, l_addr.as_u32);
       nat_6t_flow_txfib_rewrite_set (&s->o2i, rx_fib_index);
